### 1. Register a new email (Expect: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Register the same email again (Expect: 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Register with a 3-character password (Expect: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser2@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Log in with the wrong password (Expect: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser1@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 5. Log in correctly (Expect: 200 OK and a token)
# COPY THE TOKEN FROM THE RESPONSE AND PASTE IT IN @token AT THE TOP
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newuser1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 6. GET /api/issues with no token (Expect: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues

### 7. GET /api/issues with a garbage token (Expect: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues
Authorization: Bearer this_is_a_garbage_invalid_token_string

### 8. Create an issue with no title (Expect: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title test",
  "severity": "Low",
  "status": "Open"
}

### 9. Create an issue with spoofed createdBy (Expect: 201, createdBy should be YOU, not hacker)
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spoof test",
  "severity": "Medium",
  "status": "Open",
  "createdBy": "hacker@example.com"
}

### 10. GET /api/issues/abc (Expect: 400 Bad Request - Invalid Mongo ID format)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. GET a valid-looking id that doesn’t exist (Expect: 404 Not Found)
# Using a structurally valid 24-character hex string that isn't in your DB
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues/5f8d0d55b54764421b7156d9
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Update an issue (Expect: 200 OK)
# Replace the ID in the URL with a real issue ID from your database
PUT {{baseUrl}}/issues/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "In Progress"
}

### 13. Delete an issue (Expect: 200 OK or 204 No Content)
# Replace the ID in the URL with the same real issue ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/issues/6ace7576ac53f82b3a8a5dd0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Fetch the deleted issue (Expect: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues/6ace7576ac53f82b3a8a5dd0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Query Parameters: ?q=login (Expect: 200 OK, matching issues)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues?q=login
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Query Parameters: ?status=Open (Expect: 200 OK, Open issues)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues?status=Open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Query Parameters Combined (Expect: 200 OK, matching both)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues?q=login&status=Open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Regex crash test (Expect: 200 OK or empty array, NOT a 500 crash)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues?q=(
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}